    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\n```editorconfig\nroot = true\n[foo{1..1}]\n```\n\nThe EditorConfig file shown above is technically invalid according to <https://spec.editorconfig.org/#glob-expressions>:\n\n> any integer numbers between `num1` and `num2`, where `num1` and `num2` can be either positive or negative. `num1` is required to be ***less than*** `num2`.\n\n(emphasis mine)\nBut no warning is issued; Vim:E944 is issued when `num1` &gt; `num2`.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```console\n$ cat > .editorconfig << EOF\nroot = true\n[foo{1..1}]\nEOF\n$ nvim --clean foo1\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nhttps://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/e04196ea51167924c83850619bbf359665db0d0e/src/nvim/regexp.c#L10649\n\n```diff\n--- a/src/nvim/regexp.c\n+++ b/src/nvim/regexp.c\n@@ -10648,3 +10648,3 @@ collection:\n           startc = oldstartc;\n-          if (startc > endc) {\n+          if (startc >= endc) {\n             EMSG_RET_FAIL(_(e_reverse_range));\n```\n\nWith the patch applied, Vim:E944 is emitted against `{num..num}` pattern (range is not reversed though); possibly it will introduce regression, however.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\ne04196ea51167924c83850619bbf359665db0d0e\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nn/a\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nEndeavourOS\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nghostty 1.3.1\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "```ini\nroot = true\n[foo{2..10}]\n```\n\ngive error\n\n```\nError in BufReadPost Autocommands for \"*\":\nLua callback: ...unwrapped-0.12.4/share/nvim/runtime/lua/editorconfig.lua:285: couldn't parse regex: Vim:E944: Reverse range in character class\nstack traceback:\n        [C]: in function 'regex'\n        ...unwrapped-0.12.4/share/nvim/runtime/lua/editorconfig.lua:285: in function 'parse'\n        ...unwrapped-0.12.4/share/nvim/runtime/lua/editorconfig.lua:325: in function 'config'\n        ...rapped-0.12.4/share/nvim/runtime/plugin/editorconfig.lua:11: in function <...rapped-0.12.4/share/nvim/runtime/plugin/editorconfig.lua:4>\n```\n\nweird. Looks like nvim treat it as `2..1` .",
