        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Apparently using it as a glob won't work because it isn't a glob. I tried converting it to lpeg instead of regex, but [glob doesn't have numeric ranges](https://www.man7.org/linux/man-pages/man7/glob.7.html) like EditorConfig to begin with (only character class `[0-9]`, not `{0..9}`), so it still doesn't work. EditorConfig glob is its own thing, which is separate from the glob in `glob.lua`, which is separate from the vim \"glob\" (`:h wildcard`). So it seems like we need at least three glob implementations to support it properly. Nasty.",
